/* Readings for the four main asteroids: Ceres, Pallas, Juno and Vesta. */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};

window.AstroDeep.asteroids = {
  ceres: {
    overview: "In myth, Ceres (the Greek Demeter) was the goddess of grain whose daughter Persephone was taken into the underworld. In her grief Ceres let the earth go barren, until a deal was struck that returned Persephone for part of every year, and the seasons were born.\n\nIn your chart, Ceres shows how you need to be cared for and how you instinctively care for others. It describes what makes you feel fed, in the literal sense of food and the wider sense of attention, comfort and acceptance. It also points to your experience of loss and return: the attachments that are hardest to let go of, the grief that teaches you something, and the way you rebuild after something precious is taken away. Where Ceres sits, you learn that nurture includes letting go as well as holding on, and that caring for yourself is not a luxury but the ground everything else grows from.",
    gifts: ["Instinctive nurturing", "Resilience after loss", "Deep bodily wisdom"],
    challenges: ["Smothering or over-giving", "Grief that hardens into control", "Neglecting your own needs"],
    advice: "Notice what genuinely replenishes you this week, then schedule it as firmly as you would a commitment to someone else.",
    signs: {
      aries: "Ceres in Aries nurtures through encouragement and independence. You feel cared for when someone backs your right to go your own way, and you show love by pushing people to stand on their own feet. Being fussed over can feel stifling, while being cheered on feels like real warmth. You may have learned early to look after yourself, and that self-reliance is both a strength and a wound. Your nurture flows best through action: fixing, starting, defending. The lesson is to allow yourself to be looked after without reading it as a sign of weakness, and to remember that other people sometimes need soothing before they need a push.",
      taurus: "With Ceres in Taurus, care is physical, steady and sensory. Good food, a warm bed, touch, a reliable routine: these are how you feel loved and how you love. You are often a gifted cook, gardener or host, and people relax in the atmosphere you create. Stability matters so much that change can register as a threat to your wellbeing. Loss may show up around possessions, money or the body, and teach you that security runs deeper than what you own. Your healing comes through slowing down and letting your body tell you what it needs, rather than holding on to comfort out of fear.",
      gemini: "Ceres in Gemini feeds people with words, ideas and interest. You feel nurtured when someone truly listens, answers your questions and keeps the conversation going. Talking things through is how you process feeling, and you care for others by explaining, teaching, sending links and checking in with a quick message. Silence or being ignored can feel like emotional starvation. Siblings, neighbours or early schooling may be where you learned about care and its absence. The growth edge is noticing when chatter becomes a way to avoid the body, and letting some feelings be felt before they are named.",
      cancer: "Here Ceres is at home, and the urge to nurture runs deep. You are protective, attuned to moods and quick to sense when someone is hungry, tired or hurting. Family, home and belonging are central to your sense of being cared for. Your bond with your mother or main caregiver shapes you strongly, for good and ill. Loss hits hard, because you attach deeply, and you may hold on long after something has run its course. The gift is a genuine capacity to make people feel safe. The work is letting those you love grow up and away, and mothering yourself as tenderly as you mother everyone else.",
      leo: "Ceres in Leo nurtures through praise, play and generous attention. You feel cared for when you are seen, admired and delighted in, and you care for others by making them feel special. Children, creative projects and anyone who needs confidence tend to flourish around you. If love felt conditional on performance when you were young, you may still work hard to earn it. Loss can bruise your pride as much as your heart. Your healing comes through creative expression and through learning that you are worth loving on an ordinary, unremarkable day, not only when you shine.",
      virgo: "With Ceres in Virgo, care means practical help, useful service and attention to health. You nurture by fixing what is broken, tidying up, organising meals and noticing the small things others miss. You feel looked after when someone helps you in concrete ways rather than simply offering sympathy. Food, digestion and daily routines may be closely tied to your emotional state. The shadow is criticism dressed up as care, towards others or towards your own body. Growth comes when you accept that being imperfect does not make you unworthy of nurture, and when you let help be received without having to earn it.",
      libra: "Ceres in Libra finds nourishment in partnership, fairness and beauty. You feel cared for when relationships are balanced and when someone meets you as an equal. You tend to nurture by keeping the peace, smoothing over conflict and making spaces pleasant. Loss often arrives through relationships, breakups or a sense of injustice, and those experiences shape how you love afterward. You may give too much to keep harmony and then quietly resent it. The lesson is that true care sometimes requires disagreement, and that a relationship which feeds you must also leave room for your honest needs.",
      scorpio: "Ceres in Scorpio carries the Demeter and Persephone story at full intensity. Your nurture is deep, loyal and fiercely protective, and you feel cared for when someone stays with you through the darkest feelings without flinching. You may have known early losses, secrets or power struggles around care. Attachment can become control when fear of losing someone takes over. Yet you are also remarkably good at helping others through crisis, grief and transformation. Your healing comes through trusting that what is truly yours returns in some form, and that releasing your grip can be its own form of love.",
      sagittarius: "With Ceres in Sagittarius, you are nourished by freedom, meaning and adventure. You feel cared for when someone supports your growth, shares your big questions and gives you room to roam. You nurture others by widening their horizons, introducing them to new places and ideas, and encouraging faith in themselves. Being confined or lectured can feel like a lack of love. You may have learned about care through travel, religion or a teacher more than through home. The work is noticing that restlessness can be a way to avoid need, and that staying put for someone can also be an adventure.",
      capricorn: "Ceres in Capricorn nurtures through responsibility, structure and reliability. You show care by providing, planning and being the one who can be counted on. You may have grown up fast, taking on duties that left little room to be a child, so being looked after can feel unfamiliar. You feel nurtured when your efforts are respected and when someone else takes charge for a change. The risk is equating love with work and forgetting softness. Your healing comes through allowing rest without justification, and recognising that people love you for who you are, not only for what you hold together.",
      aquarius: "Ceres in Aquarius cares through acceptance, friendship and freedom from convention. You feel nourished when you are allowed to be different, and you nurture others by respecting their individuality and backing their right to be themselves. Community, chosen family and shared causes often feed you more than traditional family ties. You may have experienced care that felt distant or unusual, and so you can seem detached when feelings run high. The lesson is to let closeness in without fearing it will cost you your independence, and to offer warmth as well as understanding.",
      pisces: "With Ceres in Pisces, nurture is compassionate, intuitive and boundless. You sense suffering easily and want to soothe it, sometimes to the point of losing yourself. You feel cared for through quiet presence, music, prayer, water or time alone to dissolve and recover. Early care may have been inconsistent, idealised or tangled with someone else's sorrow. The shadow is martyrdom, or care that enables rather than heals. Your gift is unconditional acceptance. The work is putting gentle boundaries around it, so that the love you give does not drain the well you draw it from."
    },
    houses: {
      1: "Ceres in the first house makes nurture part of how you meet the world. People often experience you as caring, approachable or maternal before they know you well, and you may end up looking after others without meaning to. Your own body is a key barometer: when you are poorly fed or tired, it shows quickly. You learn about care by first learning to care for yourself, including your appearance, energy and physical needs. The challenge is not letting your identity rest entirely on being needed.",
      2: "In the second house, Ceres links nurture with resources, money and self-worth. Feeling materially secure is a large part of feeling cared for, and you often show love through gifts, food or financial support. Episodes of loss or scarcity may have shaped your values. You have a gift for growing things slowly, whether savings, gardens or skills. The work is recognising that your worth is not measured by what you can provide, and that you deserve care even when you have nothing to offer in return.",
      3: "Ceres in the third house nurtures through communication, learning and everyday connection. Siblings, neighbours and early schooling may have been important places of care or its lack. You tend to look after people by talking with them, teaching them and keeping them informed. A good conversation can feel as nourishing as a meal. You may carry an old hunger to be heard. Growth comes from choosing your words kindly, including the ones you use inside your own head.",
      4: "With Ceres in the fourth house, home and family are central to how you give and receive care. The relationship with a parent, often the mother, is formative and may involve a strong bond, a loss or a role reversal. You are likely to create a nourishing home and to feel unsettled when your base is unstable. Your roots, ancestry and private life carry emotional weight. The task is to build inner security that does not depend on everything at home staying the same.",
      5: "Ceres in the fifth house nurtures through play, creativity and children. You may be naturally good with young people, or your creative work may feel like something you have birthed and raised. Joy and self-expression are forms of self-care for you. Loss can come around children, romance or creative projects, and teaches you to love without owning. The lesson is to let what you create find its own life, and to allow yourself to play without needing to take care of anyone.",
      6: "Ceres in the sixth house brings nurture into daily work, health and service. Routines around food, sleep and movement strongly affect your wellbeing. You may be drawn to caring professions, nutrition, healing or looking after animals. You tend to show love through helpful acts and feel cared for when someone makes your daily load lighter. The risk is overwork in the name of being useful. Your health improves when self-care becomes a daily practice rather than an emergency measure.",
      7: "In the seventh house, Ceres puts nurture at the heart of partnership. You may attract partners who need looking after, or who look after you, and the balance of care is a recurring theme. Relationships can feel like family. Losses in partnership are deeply felt and often transformative. You learn the difference between caring for someone and managing them. The healthiest bonds are those where both people feed each other and both are free to leave and return.",
      8: "Ceres in the eighth house holds the Persephone myth close. Themes of loss, grief, inheritance and transformation run through your experience of care. You may have faced separation early, or learned about love through crisis. Intimacy and shared resources can bring up fears of being consumed or abandoned. Yet you have a rare ability to support others through death, endings and deep change. Your healing comes through trusting cycles: what goes under does come back, in a changed form.",
      9: "Ceres in the ninth house nurtures through meaning, faith and exploration. You may find care through teachers, travel, philosophy or a spiritual tradition, and you feed others by sharing wisdom and widening their world. Foreign cultures and foods can feel strangely like home. There may be a loss of faith, or of a homeland, that reshapes your beliefs. The lesson is to keep your nourishing ideas open to question, so they stay alive rather than rigid.",
      10: "With Ceres in the tenth house, nurture becomes part of your public role or career. You may work in caring, feeding, teaching or healing fields, or be seen as a protective figure in your community. A parent's example of care, or its absence, strongly shapes your ambitions. Recognition matters, and you may feel starved when your contribution goes unnoticed. The work is making sure your caring role in the world does not leave your private needs unmet.",
      11: "Ceres in the eleventh house finds nourishment through friendship, groups and shared ideals. Friends may be your chosen family, and you often take on a caring role in teams or communities. You care about causes that feed people, protect the vulnerable or improve collective wellbeing. Losses may come through friendships changing or groups dissolving. Growth comes when you let friends care for you too, rather than always being the one who holds the group together.",
      12: "In the twelfth house, Ceres works quietly and often invisibly. You may care for others behind the scenes, in hospitals, retreats, institutions or through private sacrifice. Your own need for nurture can be hidden, even from yourself, and early care may have involved absence, illness or unspoken grief. Solitude, sleep, dreams and spiritual practice replenish you. The task is to bring your needs into the light, and to accept care without guilt."
    },
    aspects: {
      fusion: "A conjunction fuses the planet's function with Ceres, so that energy becomes a primary way you nurture and need to be nurtured. It also ties that planet to themes of attachment, loss and return.",
      harmony: "Trines and sextiles let care flow easily through the planet's qualities. You can draw on this area of life to feed yourself and others without much struggle.",
      tension: "Squares and oppositions set up friction between your need for care and what the planet demands. The tension often shows as over-giving, control or neglect until you find a way to honour both sides.",
      adjust: "A quincunx asks for constant small adjustments between how you nurture and what the planet needs, often showing up through health or daily routines.",
      creative: "A quintile gives a distinctive, inventive talent for expressing care through the planet's qualities."
    },
    dominant: "When Ceres is prominent, conjunct the Sun, Moon or an angle, nurture becomes a central thread of your life story. You may be seen as a natural carer, feeder, healer or protector, and questions of food, the body, parenting and self-care take on real weight. Loss and return may also be defining experiences, teaching you about attachment and letting go. The gift is a powerful capacity to help people and things grow. The work is making sure the caring flows both ways, so that you are nourished as fully as those you tend."
  },
  pallas: {
    overview: "Pallas Athena sprang fully armed from the head of her father Zeus. She was the goddess of wisdom, strategy, crafts and just warfare, a protector of cities and heroes who preferred intelligence to brute force.\n\nIn your chart, Pallas shows how your mind sees patterns and solves problems. It describes your strategic intelligence, the kind of creative wisdom that grasps the whole picture at once, and your sense of justice. It also points to how you relate to the masculine and the world of the father, especially if you are a woman who learned early to be clever, capable and perhaps a little armoured. Pallas often governs the healing arts, design, activism and any skill where perception turns into craft. Where Pallas sits, you can see what others miss. The challenge is to use that insight without cutting yourself off from feeling, intimacy or softness in the process.",
    gifts: ["Pattern recognition", "Strategic problem solving", "A clear sense of justice"],
    challenges: ["Living in the head", "Armouring the heart", "Winning the argument, losing the connection"],
    advice: "When you spot the solution to a problem, pause and ask how the people involved feel before you present it.",
    signs: {
      aries: "Pallas in Aries thinks fast and strategises on the move. Your intelligence works best under pressure, when there is a challenge to meet or a wrong to put right. You see the quickest route through a problem and act on it before others have finished discussing. You may be a natural advocate, fighting for underdogs and causes with courage and directness. The risk is treating every disagreement as a battle to be won. Your wisdom deepens when you let a situation breathe for a moment, so your first brilliant instinct can be tested against a second, calmer look.",
      taurus: "With Pallas in Taurus, your intelligence is practical, patient and grounded in the senses. You recognise patterns in materials, money, bodies and the natural world, and your best ideas take solid form: a design, a garden, a business, a crafted object. You prefer strategies that last over clever shortcuts. Healing through touch, food or bodywork may come naturally. The shadow is stubbornness, holding to a plan long after the evidence has changed. Your wisdom grows when you trust your steady instincts while staying willing to revise the blueprint.",
      gemini: "Pallas in Gemini gives a quick, agile, connecting mind. You spot links between ideas, people and information that others overlook, and you can explain complex things simply. Writing, teaching, debate, languages and networking are natural outlets for your strategic gift. You may solve problems by talking them through or by gathering many viewpoints. The risk is scattering your brilliance across too many threads, or using cleverness to dodge feeling. Your wisdom matures when you follow one line of enquiry deeply enough to turn information into real understanding.",
      cancer: "Here Pallas brings intelligence to the service of protection and belonging. You read emotional patterns with unusual accuracy and often know what a family, team or community needs before anyone says it. Your strategies tend to be about keeping people safe. There may be tension between being clever and being caring, perhaps from a family where one was valued over the other. The healing arts, especially those that nurture, can suit you well. Your growth comes from trusting that your feelings are a source of intelligence, not something that clouds it.",
      leo: "Pallas in Leo expresses wisdom through creativity, performance and leadership. You have a strong sense of design and drama, and you see how to present an idea so that it inspires people. Your strategic mind often works in the service of a vision you believe in wholeheartedly. You may have sought a father's approval by being bright and impressive. The risk is needing credit for every insight. Your wisdom becomes generous when you use your creative intelligence to help others shine as well.",
      virgo: "With Pallas in Virgo, your intelligence is precise, analytical and focused on improvement. You spot the flaw in the system, the error in the data, the small change that would make everything work better. Health, craft, editing and technical skill are natural homes for your gift. You often heal through careful attention to detail. The shadow is perfectionism and a sharp critical eye turned too often on yourself. Your wisdom grows when you accept that a good enough solution delivered today often helps more than a perfect one that never arrives.",
      libra: "Pallas in Libra gives a strategic mind for fairness, diplomacy and design. You see the balance points in any situation and can find solutions that satisfy several sides. Law, mediation, the arts and partnership work are natural fields for your intelligence. You may have a strong eye for proportion and beauty. The risk is weighing every option so carefully that you never commit, or keeping the peace at the cost of justice. Your wisdom matures when you are willing to take a clear stand for what is fair, even if it disturbs the harmony.",
      scorpio: "Pallas in Scorpio thinks strategically in the dark. You read hidden motives, power dynamics and psychological patterns with piercing accuracy. Research, investigation, psychology and crisis work can suit you well, because you are unafraid of what lies beneath the surface. You may have learned to protect yourself through intelligence, keeping your cards close. The shadow is using insight to control or to win. Your wisdom deepens when you use what you perceive to heal and empower others rather than to guard against them.",
      sagittarius: "With Pallas in Sagittarius, your intelligence works through the big picture. You grasp philosophies, systems of belief and cultural patterns quickly, and you can see where a situation is heading long before others. Teaching, publishing, law, travel and activism may call to you. You are often an advocate for truth and freedom. The risk is broad strokes that miss the details, or certainty that becomes preachy. Your wisdom grows when you ground your vision in facts and remain curious about views that differ from yours.",
      capricorn: "Pallas in Capricorn gives a strategic, organised, long-range mind. You see how systems and institutions work and how to build something that lasts. Leadership, planning, management and structural design come naturally. You may have absorbed a strong paternal sense of duty and achievement. The shadow is becoming so focused on competence that you forget warmth. Your wisdom matures when you let your authority include empathy, and when you recognise that the most enduring structures leave room for human needs. You are often the quiet strategist others rely on when the stakes are high.",
      aquarius: "Pallas in Aquarius is original, inventive and future-minded. You see patterns across whole systems and societies, and your ideas often seem ahead of their time. Technology, science, social reform and group strategy are natural outlets. You care about justice on a collective scale. The risk is detachment, treating people as parts of a model rather than as individuals with feelings. Your wisdom deepens when you let your brilliance serve real human relationships, not just abstract ideals. Your best insights often arrive as sudden flashes that reorganise everything you thought you knew.",
      pisces: "With Pallas in Pisces, your intelligence is intuitive, imaginative and holistic. You grasp patterns through images, dreams, music and feeling rather than through logic alone, and your insights can seem to arrive from nowhere. Healing, the arts and spiritual work are natural fields. You may find it hard to explain how you know what you know. The shadow is doubting your own perceptions or letting them drift into fantasy. Your wisdom grows when you test your intuitions against reality and then trust the ones that hold."
    },
    houses: {
      1: "Pallas in the first house makes intelligence part of your visible identity. People see you as clever, capable or strategic, and you may meet the world with a certain armour. You often solve problems for others instinctively. There can be a tension between being admired for your mind and wanting to be approached with softness. The work is letting people see the feeling person behind the quick perception. A useful practice is saying \"I don't know yet\" out loud, and noticing that people still respect you.",
      2: "In the second house, Pallas brings strategic intelligence to money, resources and values. You can see how to build income, design a business or make practical skills pay. Your self-worth may be closely tied to being competent. You may be drawn to crafts that turn wisdom into something tangible. Growth comes when you value yourself for more than your usefulness and cleverness. You often see the value in overlooked things, and can turn a simple idea into a steady living.",
      3: "Pallas in the third house gives a sharp, pattern-seeking mind for communication, writing and learning. You may excel at explaining, debating or teaching, and siblings or early schooling could have been where your intelligence was first recognised or tested. Everyday problem solving comes easily. The challenge is making sure your quickness does not make others feel slow or unheard. Try asking one more question before offering your answer, and you may learn something the pattern missed.",
      4: "With Pallas in the fourth house, your strategic intelligence is tied to home, family and roots. The father or a parent may have strongly shaped how you think, perhaps prizing achievement or reason. You may be the one who organises and protects the family. Your deepest insights often come from understanding your background. The work is building a home where both wisdom and tenderness are welcome. You may also be the family member who sees the patterns everyone else has quietly agreed not to name.",
      5: "Pallas in the fifth house channels intelligence into creativity, play and romance. Your creative work often has a clever, well-designed quality, and you may enjoy games of strategy. You might be drawn to partners who admire your mind. With children, you can be an inspiring teacher. The risk is overthinking pleasure. Your growth comes from allowing yourself to create simply for the joy of it. Games, puzzles and design projects can be where your mind finally relaxes and plays.",
      6: "In the sixth house, Pallas applies wisdom to daily work, health and service. You are good at improving systems, diagnosing problems and finding practical solutions. The healing arts, analysis or technical roles may suit you. You may approach your own health like a puzzle to be solved. The shadow is overwork and nitpicking. Balance comes when you let your routines include rest and play as well as efficiency. Colleagues often bring you the problems nobody else can crack.",
      7: "Pallas in the seventh house brings strategy into partnership. You may attract clever partners, or become the thinker and planner in relationships. Mediation, law, consulting and advisory roles can suit you. There may be a pattern of intellectual rivalry or of being valued more for your mind than your heart. The lesson is to let relationships be places where you can be vulnerable, not just brilliant. Notice whether you choose partners you can outthink, and whether that keeps you safe or keeps you lonely.",
      8: "Pallas in the eighth house gives insight into hidden matters: psychology, power, shared resources, sexuality and death. You can see what lies beneath a situation and plan wisely in a crisis. Research, finance, therapy and investigation may draw you. You may protect yourself by understanding everything. Healing comes when you let yourself be touched as well as knowing. In a crisis you are often the calmest person in the room, quietly working out the next three moves.",
      9: "With Pallas in the ninth house, your intelligence is drawn to philosophy, law, higher education, travel and belief. You can grasp whole worldviews and see how ideas fit together. Teaching, publishing or advocacy may be your calling. You might fight for justice on a broad scale. The risk is intellectual pride. Your wisdom grows through staying a student even as you teach. Your sense of justice can widen into a commitment to people far beyond your own circle.",
      10: "Pallas in the tenth house makes strategic intelligence part of your career and public image. You may be known as an expert, adviser, leader or advocate. The father or a mentor may have shaped your ambitions. You tend to rise through competence and clear thinking. The work is making sure your professional armour does not become the whole of who you are. A mentor who treats you as capable, rather than merely useful, can change the whole direction of your working life.",
      11: "In the eleventh house, Pallas brings strategy to groups, networks and social causes. You can see how a community could work better and help organise it. Activism, technology, science and collaborative projects may draw you. Friends often value your insight. The challenge is staying connected to individual friendships rather than only to the ideals you share. You are often the person who quietly turns a group's good intentions into a workable plan.",
      12: "Pallas in the twelfth house works through intuition, dreams and hidden channels. Your intelligence may operate quietly, and you might not always get credit for your insights. Healing, spiritual work, research or behind-the-scenes strategy can suit you. You may doubt your own mind, especially if it was not valued early on. Growth comes when you trust the wisdom that arrives in silence. Journalling, meditation or simply walking alone often reveal solutions your busy mind could not reach."
    },
    aspects: {
      fusion: "A conjunction merges the planet's energy with your strategic and creative intelligence, so that area of life becomes a vehicle for pattern recognition and problem solving. It can also bring father or justice themes to the fore.",
      harmony: "Trines and sextiles let your wisdom flow smoothly through the planet's qualities. Ideas become practical solutions with relative ease.",
      tension: "Squares and oppositions create friction between clear thinking and the planet's needs, often showing as a split between head and heart or a struggle for justice. Working through it sharpens your insight considerably.",
      adjust: "A quincunx asks you to keep adjusting how your intelligence and the planet's energy work together, often through trial and error.",
      creative: "A quintile gives a rare creative gift for designing clever solutions through the planet's qualities."
    },
    dominant: "When Pallas is prominent, conjunct the Sun, Moon or an angle, intelligence and strategy become central to your identity. You may be known for seeing the pattern, solving the problem or fighting for fairness. Themes around the father, authority and gender roles often run strongly through your story, and you may have learned early to lead with your mind. The healing arts, design, law and activism can be powerful outlets. The work is integrating your brilliance with your capacity for intimacy, so that wisdom includes the heart."
  },
  juno: {
    overview: "Juno (the Greek Hera) was the wife of Jupiter and the goddess of marriage. Her marriage was famously difficult: she endured his constant infidelity and responded with jealousy and fury, yet she never left, standing for the sacred commitment she embodied.\n\nIn your chart, Juno shows what you need to feel truly partnered. It describes the kind of committed relationship that satisfies you, what makes you feel respected as an equal, and the qualities you look for in a long-term partner. It also shows how you handle the harder side of commitment: jealousy, betrayal, power imbalance and the fear of being taken for granted. Juno is less about romance and more about the lasting bond, including business partnerships and deep friendships. Where Juno sits, you learn what loyalty means to you, what you will and will not tolerate, and how to keep your own power while sharing a life with someone else.",
    gifts: ["Deep loyalty", "Commitment to equality", "Capacity for lasting partnership"],
    challenges: ["Jealousy and possessiveness", "Staying too long in unequal bonds", "Power struggles"],
    advice: "Write down what equality looks like to you in a relationship, then check honestly whether your closest partnership meets it.",
    signs: {
      aries: "Juno in Aries needs a partnership that respects your independence and your drive. You feel most committed when your partner is a peer who can meet your energy, handle direct conflict and let you lead sometimes. A relationship that feels dull or passive will not hold you. You may be drawn to bold, active partners. The shadow is impatience or competition inside the relationship, with both people trying to win. Commitment deepens when you learn that being a team does not threaten your autonomy, and that cooling off before reacting keeps the bond strong.",
      taurus: "With Juno in Taurus, commitment is built on stability, loyalty and shared comfort. You need a partner who is reliable, physically affectionate and willing to build something steady over time. Financial security and a pleasant home can feel like part of the marriage vow. Once committed, you tend to stay. The shadow is possessiveness or treating a partner as something you own. Your relationships flourish when security includes room for change, and when loyalty is a choice renewed rather than a habit clung to.",
      gemini: "Juno in Gemini needs a partner who is also a friend and a conversation companion. Mental connection, shared curiosity and constant communication keep your commitment alive. You may need variety and freedom within the relationship, and an unusual arrangement can suit you. Boredom is the real threat. The shadow is restlessness or keeping options open to avoid depth. Partnership deepens when you let conversation lead somewhere vulnerable, and when you trust that one person can hold your interest if you both keep learning.",
      cancer: "Here Juno seeks a partnership that feels like home. You need emotional safety, nurture and a sense of family, and you are deeply loyal once you feel secure. A partner who is protective and domestic, or who welcomes your care, suits you. You may find it hard to leave, even when a bond is not serving you, because the attachment runs so deep. Jealousy can come from fear of abandonment. Your growth comes from building inner security, so that commitment is a choice made freely rather than a need driven by fear.",
      leo: "Juno in Leo needs to feel adored, admired and proud of the partnership. You want a relationship with warmth, romance and a sense of occasion, and a partner who celebrates you publicly. Loyalty matters enormously, and any hint of being overlooked or replaced can wound deeply. You tend to be generous and devoted in return. The shadow is pride or needing constant attention. Your relationships flourish when you both shine and both make room for the other to shine too.",
      virgo: "With Juno in Virgo, you show commitment through practical care and daily devotion. You need a partner who is dependable, thoughtful and willing to work on the relationship. Shared routines, helping each other and improving your life together build the bond. You may be attracted to capable, modest people. The shadow is criticism, or a sense that the relationship has become more duty than joy. Partnership deepens when you accept imperfection in your partner and yourself, and remember to appreciate as well as improve.",
      libra: "Juno in Libra is in a natural home, and partnership is central to your life. You need fairness, harmony and a partner who treats you as a genuine equal. Beauty, courtesy and shared social life matter. You are highly sensitive to imbalance and may feel betrayed when the scales tip. The shadow is avoiding conflict to keep the peace, which lets resentment build. Your relationships thrive when you speak up early about what feels unfair, trusting that honesty is part of harmony.",
      scorpio: "Juno in Scorpio seeks a bond of total intimacy and depth. You need a partner who is loyal, emotionally honest and unafraid of intensity. Commitment for you is almost a merging, and trust is everything. Betrayal can feel unforgivable. Themes of jealousy, control and shared power are likely to arise, sometimes painfully. Yet your capacity for transformation through partnership is profound. The work is building trust without trying to control, and letting both people keep some private space within the bond.",
      sagittarius: "With Juno in Sagittarius, you need a partnership built on freedom, growth and shared meaning. A partner who is adventurous, honest and interested in the big questions keeps you engaged. Travel, learning and shared beliefs can bind you together. Feeling fenced in is a relationship killer. The shadow is avoiding the everyday work of commitment or expecting a partner to be a guru. Your relationships flourish when you treat commitment itself as an adventure, and grow alongside each other rather than apart.",
      capricorn: "Juno in Capricorn takes commitment seriously. You need a partner who is responsible, ambitious and willing to build a solid life together. Status, stability and long-term planning matter, and you may be drawn to older or more established partners. Once committed, you are dependable and enduring. The shadow is a relationship that becomes more about duty or image than affection. Your partnerships deepen when you allow tenderness and play alongside the shared goals. Commitment, for you, is something you prove over years rather than declare in a moment.",
      aquarius: "Juno in Aquarius needs a partnership of equals with plenty of freedom. You are drawn to unusual, independent partners and may prefer a relationship that does not follow the standard script. Friendship is the foundation of commitment for you. You value honesty over sentimentality. The shadow is emotional distance or resisting closeness in the name of independence. Your relationships flourish when you let yourself be truly intimate while keeping the freedom you both need. You need to know that your partner would still choose you if nothing obliged them to.",
      pisces: "With Juno in Pisces, you seek a spiritual, romantic and compassionate union. You want a partner who feels like a soulmate and who understands you without words. Your devotion can be selfless and deeply healing. The shadow is idealising a partner, rescuing them, or staying with someone out of pity. Boundaries can blur. Your relationships thrive when compassion is balanced with clear sight, so that you love the real person rather than the dream of them. Your partnerships can be a genuine spiritual path when both people stay honest."
    },
    houses: {
      1: "Juno in the first house makes partnership part of your identity. You may define yourself strongly through your relationships, or marry young, or be seen as a committed partner type. You project loyalty and seriousness about relationships. The challenge is remaining your own person inside a partnership, so that commitment expands your identity rather than replacing it. You may also be quick to notice unfairness in other people's relationships, and to speak up about it. Your own partnerships work best when your partner loves your independence as much as your loyalty.",
      2: "In the second house, Juno links commitment with money, values and security. Financial partnership may be important, and shared resources can be a source of both bonding and conflict. You need a partner whose values match yours. The lesson is to keep your own financial and emotional footing, so that security within the relationship is shared, not dependent. Talking openly about money early in a relationship saves you a great deal of hurt later. You may also notice that how a partner treats your possessions and time tells you how they value you.",
      3: "Juno in the third house needs communication at the heart of partnership. You want a partner you can talk with endlessly, and you may meet partners through study, writing or local connections. Siblings may influence your view of commitment. The risk is that talking replaces feeling. Partnership thrives when words carry both honesty and warmth. A partner who texts back, remembers what you said and wants to hear about your day earns your loyalty. Silence or poor communication can feel like a breach of trust.",
      4: "With Juno in the fourth house, commitment is closely tied to home and family. You may want a traditional domestic partnership, or find that your family patterns shape how you commit. A partner may become like family, or family obligations may affect the relationship. The work is building a home with your partner that reflects both of your needs, not just inherited expectations. You may also be drawn to partners who remind you of a parent, for better or worse, until you choose consciously.",
      5: "Juno in the fifth house brings romance, creativity and play into commitment. You want a partnership that stays fun, passionate and expressive, and children may be an important part of the bond. You may seek a partner who admires your creativity. The risk is losing interest when the romance fades. Commitment deepens when you keep playfulness alive through the ordinary days. You may also feel jealousy most sharply around attention, affection or a partner's admiration for someone else.",
      6: "In the sixth house, Juno links partnership with work, health and daily life. You may meet a partner through work, or share a working partnership. Daily routines and practical help matter a great deal. The shadow is a relationship that becomes all tasks and no tenderness. The bond thrives when you make time for pleasure alongside shared responsibilities. You may also notice that small daily courtesies, or their absence, reveal far more than grand gestures. A fair division of chores is part of equality for you.",
      7: "Juno in the seventh house is strongly placed, making committed partnership a central life theme. You long for a true equal and take relationships seriously, including business partnerships. Fairness and loyalty matter enormously. You may learn a great deal through partners, including through conflict. The work is making sure you bring a whole self to partnership rather than looking for completion in someone else. Contracts, agreements and clear expectations can protect both people, whether in love or business.",
      8: "Juno in the eighth house seeks a bond of deep intimacy, shared power and transformation. Relationships may involve intense emotional and sexual connection, and joint finances can be significant. Jealousy and control may arise. You are capable of profound loyalty. The lesson is trust built on honesty rather than surveillance, so that the depth you crave can feel safe. You may also find that major life changes, including loss or inheritance, test and ultimately strengthen your commitments.",
      9: "With Juno in the ninth house, you need a partner who shares your values, beliefs or sense of adventure. You may partner with someone from another culture, or meet through travel or study. Growth together is essential. The risk is expecting a partner to supply meaning. The bond thrives when you both keep exploring, together and separately. Legal matters, weddings abroad or a shared spiritual practice may mark important chapters in your partnerships. Honest disagreement about beliefs can make the bond stronger rather than weaker.",
      10: "Juno in the tenth house links partnership with career, status and public life. You may work with a partner, or choose a partner who supports your ambitions or brings standing. Your relationship may be visible to others. The challenge is ensuring the partnership is about love as well as image, and that neither career overshadows the other. You may also carry a strong sense that your partner reflects on you, which adds pressure to choose well. Choose for private happiness first.",
      11: "In the eleventh house, Juno seeks a partner who is also a friend. You may meet partners through groups or shared causes, and you value a relationship that respects your independence and ideals. Unconventional arrangements may suit you. Growth comes when friendship deepens into real emotional commitment rather than staying comfortable at a distance. You may need a partner who supports your friendships and causes, and who does not feel threatened by your wider circle.",
      12: "Juno in the twelfth house can bring hidden, spiritual or sacrificial elements to partnership. You may idealise partners, keep relationships private, or feel a karmic pull to someone. There can be themes of loss, secrecy or caring for a partner. The work is bringing your relationship needs into the open and making sure devotion does not turn into self-erasure. Therapy, spiritual practice or honest journalling can help you see a partner clearly rather than through a haze of longing."
    },
    aspects: {
      fusion: "A conjunction merges the planet's energy with your need for committed partnership, so that quality becomes something you seek in or bring to a long-term bond. It can intensify themes of loyalty and power.",
      harmony: "Trines and sextiles help the planet support your partnerships, making commitment feel natural in this area of life.",
      tension: "Squares and oppositions create friction between your need for equal partnership and the planet's drives, often showing as power struggles, jealousy or recurring relationship lessons that build real maturity.",
      adjust: "A quincunx asks you to keep adjusting what you need from partnership against what the planet demands, often through small ongoing compromises.",
      creative: "A quintile gives a distinctive, creative approach to commitment shaped by the planet's qualities."
    },
    dominant: "When Juno is prominent, conjunct the Sun, Moon or an angle, committed partnership becomes a defining theme of your life. Marriage, business partnership and questions of loyalty and equality carry real weight, and you may be highly sensitive to power dynamics in relationships. You might advocate for fairness, especially for people who are overlooked or undervalued. The gift is a deep capacity for devoted, lasting bonds. The work is holding your own power inside those bonds, so that commitment is between equals rather than an arrangement you endure."
  },
  vesta: {
    overview: "Vesta (the Greek Hestia) was the virgin goddess of the hearth. Her sacred flame burned at the centre of every home and temple, tended by priestesses who dedicated their lives to her and belonged to no man.\n\nIn your chart, Vesta shows where you give yourself completely. It describes the work, practice or calling that you devote yourself to with focus and purity of intention, the inner flame you need to protect. Vesta also speaks about sexuality: sometimes as something sacred, sometimes as something channelled into other devotions, and sometimes as a place where you need to keep part of yourself private. There is a strong need for solitude and self-containment here, a sense that you must belong to yourself before you can belong to anyone. Where Vesta sits, you can concentrate with remarkable intensity. The challenge is avoiding isolation, workaholism or a narrowing of life, and remembering that the flame needs to warm people as well as illuminate the work.",
    gifts: ["Deep focus", "Devotion to a calling", "Self-containment"],
    challenges: ["Isolation", "Workaholism", "Split between intimacy and devotion"],
    advice: "Protect one block of undisturbed time each day for the work that matters most to you, and treat it as sacred.",
    signs: {
      aries: "Vesta in Aries devotes itself to pioneering and independent action. You focus most intensely when you are starting something new or working alone on your own terms. Your inner flame is courage, and you may feel called to lead or to break new ground. Sexuality can be direct and spontaneous, or channelled into physical and competitive pursuits. The risk is burning brightly and then burning out. Your devotion lasts when you learn to pace yourself and keep returning to the flame rather than rushing to the next fire.",
      taurus: "With Vesta in Taurus, your devotion is steady, sensual and practical. You focus deeply on work that produces something tangible and lasting: crafts, gardens, music, building or money. The body and the natural world feel sacred to you. Sexuality may be slow, sensuous and deeply connected to trust. You can work with remarkable patience. The shadow is becoming rigid or attached to routines that no longer serve. Your flame stays alive when you let pleasure be part of the devotion, not a reward held back until the work is done.",
      gemini: "Vesta in Gemini devotes itself to ideas, words and learning. You focus intensely on reading, writing, research or teaching, and you may be dedicated to a particular field of knowledge. Your mind is the temple. Sexuality may be expressed through wit, conversation or mental connection. The risk is scattered focus, many projects started and few completed. Your devotion deepens when you choose one subject or craft and commit to going all the way with it. A notebook, a library card or a long course of study can become a quiet form of worship.",
      cancer: "Here Vesta tends the hearth of home and family. You focus deeply on caring for loved ones, creating a sanctuary or preserving family and cultural traditions. Home is a sacred space for you, and you may need a private retreat within it. Sexuality can be tender and tied closely to emotional safety. The shadow is giving so much to family that there is nothing left for your own calling. Your flame burns best when your devotion includes yourself as one of the people you care for.",
      leo: "Vesta in Leo devotes itself to creative expression. You focus with great intensity on art, performance or anything that lets your heart shine. Creativity feels like a sacred act, and you may pour yourself into it completely. Sexuality can be warm, expressive and playful, or channelled into creative work. The risk is tying your worth to the success of your creations. Your devotion stays pure when you create for the love of it, and let applause be a bonus rather than the point.",
      virgo: "With Vesta in Virgo, devotion shows through service, skill and careful work. You focus deeply on perfecting a craft, improving systems or helping others through practical care. Health, healing and daily ritual can feel sacred. Vesta is at home here, and you may have a strong sense of purity and order. Sexuality can be private and discerning. The shadow is perfectionism and overwork. Your flame is best tended when you treat rest as part of the ritual. Small, repeated acts done well can feel like prayer to you.",
      libra: "Vesta in Libra devotes itself to relationships, beauty and justice. You may dedicate yourself to a partner, to the arts or to the cause of fairness. There can be a tension between your need for solitude and your need for partnership, and you may need a relationship that honours your private space. Sexuality is often refined and linked to harmony. The risk is losing yourself in a partner. Your devotion thrives when you tend your own flame while sharing your life.",
      scorpio: "Vesta in Scorpio devotes itself to depth, transformation and truth. You focus with intense concentration on research, healing, psychology or anything that uncovers hidden realities. Sexuality can feel powerfully sacred, a doorway to transformation, or it may be sublimated into your work. You need privacy and control over who sees your inner life. The shadow is obsession or secrecy. Your flame burns cleanly when your intensity serves healing rather than control. You may keep your deepest commitments entirely private, which gives them their power.",
      sagittarius: "With Vesta in Sagittarius, your devotion is to truth, meaning and exploration. You focus deeply on philosophy, spirituality, teaching, travel or a cause you believe in. You may feel called to a spiritual path or a lifelong quest for understanding. Sexuality can be adventurous, or channelled into a sense of mission. The risk is fanaticism or restlessness that prevents deep focus. Your flame is steadiest when you let your beliefs keep growing rather than hardening into dogma. A pilgrimage, literal or inner, can reignite your sense of purpose.",
      capricorn: "Vesta in Capricorn devotes itself to work, achievement and responsibility. You focus with great discipline on your career, a long-term goal or building something that will outlast you. Your work often feels like a vocation. Sexuality may be reserved, or channelled into ambition. The shadow is workaholism and emotional isolation. Your devotion becomes nourishing when you let people into the structure you build, and when success includes connection. You may be the person who keeps showing up long after others have lost interest, and that steadiness is its own kind of devotion.",
      aquarius: "Vesta in Aquarius devotes itself to ideals, innovation and the collective good. You focus intensely on causes, communities, science or future-oriented projects. You may feel called to serve humanity in some way. Sexuality can be unconventional, or detached from traditional expectations. The risk is devoting yourself to ideas while neglecting the people close to you. Your flame warms when you bring your ideals into your personal relationships too. You may also need long periods of independent work, where you can think without interruption and follow an idea wherever it leads.",
      pisces: "With Vesta in Pisces, your devotion is spiritual, compassionate and imaginative. You focus deeply on meditation, art, music, healing or service to those who suffer. Solitude and retreat feel essential. Sexuality can be mystical, idealised or sublimated into spiritual practice. The shadow is escaping into devotion to avoid ordinary life. Your flame burns best when your spiritual focus is grounded in daily practice and clear boundaries. You may also be unusually sensitive to atmosphere, needing quiet, clean spaces to reconnect with your inner flame. Music or water can bring you back to yourself quickly."
    },
    houses: {
      1: "Vesta in the first house makes focus and devotion part of your identity. You may come across as serious, self-contained or dedicated, and people sense the intensity of your inner flame. You need time alone to stay centred. The challenge is making sure your self-containment does not keep others at a distance they cannot cross. You may seem more private than you are, simply because so much of your energy goes inward. When you are aligned with your purpose, your presence becomes quietly magnetic and people trust your steadiness.",
      2: "In the second house, Vesta devotes itself to building resources and living by clear values. You may focus intensely on work that brings security, or treat money and possessions with careful stewardship. Your values can feel sacred. The work is making sure the pursuit of security does not crowd out the other things you hold dear. You may also be skilled at working with little, turning modest resources into something lasting through patience. Simplicity, rather than accumulation, often brings you the deepest sense of security and peace.",
      3: "Vesta in the third house focuses on communication, learning and ideas. You may be devoted to writing, teaching or a particular subject, and you can study with great concentration. Siblings or local community may be important. The risk is getting lost in your head. Balance comes from sharing what you learn rather than keeping it to yourself. You may find that a daily writing or reading habit steadies you more than anything else. Short trips or quiet walks can also clear your mind and help you return to your focus refreshed.",
      4: "With Vesta in the fourth house, home is your temple. You need a private sanctuary and may devote much of yourself to family, roots or tradition. Working from home can suit you. You may carry a family flame, a craft or value passed down. The work is making your home a place of warmth, not only of retreat. A dedicated room, corner or ritual at home helps you stay connected to what matters. You may also feel most yourself when you can close the door and be undisturbed for a while.",
      5: "Vesta in the fifth house devotes itself to creativity, children or a beloved pursuit. You focus intensely on creative projects and may treat them as a calling. Romance can be serious or kept separate from your creative life. The risk is losing the playfulness in your devotion. Your flame is brightest when creativity stays joyful. You may pour yourself into one creative passion for years, and that commitment is where your mastery comes from. With children, you can be a devoted parent or mentor who takes their gifts seriously.",
      6: "In the sixth house, Vesta is very much at home. You devote yourself to work, health and service, and you may find meaning in daily ritual and craft. You can work with remarkable focus. The shadow is burnout and a life that is all duty. Your wellbeing depends on treating rest as sacred as work. You may find a sense of the sacred in simple tasks done with full attention, such as cooking, cleaning or tending plants. Choosing work that genuinely matters to you makes all the difference to your energy.",
      7: "Vesta in the seventh house brings devotion into partnership. You may dedicate yourself to a partner or share a calling with them, yet you also need space and independence within the relationship. There can be tension between commitment and solitude. The lesson is to find a partnership that honours both your flame and your need to be close. Separate rooms, separate interests or regular time apart can actually strengthen your closeness. You may also be drawn to partners who have their own strong sense of purpose and respect yours.",
      8: "Vesta in the eighth house focuses on depth, intimacy and transformation. Sexuality can feel sacred, and you may be devoted to healing, research or work involving shared resources. You need privacy and trust. The shadow is withdrawing from intimacy altogether. Your flame is tended through honest, trusted connection. You may keep your inner life closely guarded, sharing it only with a few people who have earned deep trust. Periods of celibacy or intense privacy can be chosen rather than imposed, and can be renewing. When you do open up, the connection can be profound and lasting.",
      9: "With Vesta in the ninth house, you are devoted to a spiritual path, philosophy, study or travel. You may feel called to teach, write or follow a quest for meaning. Your beliefs are deeply held. The risk is rigid conviction. Your devotion stays alive when it keeps you curious. Long periods of study, pilgrimage or time abroad can feel like a vocation in themselves. You may also be a devoted teacher, passing on what you have learned with great seriousness. Sharing your questions, not only your answers, keeps your inner flame bright.",
      10: "Vesta in the tenth house makes your career a calling. You may devote yourself entirely to your work and be known for your dedication and expertise. Your public role can feel sacred. The shadow is workaholism and neglecting personal life. Balance comes from remembering that you are more than your vocation. You may be seen as a specialist whose standards are uncompromising. Letting colleagues and loved ones share in your purpose makes the path less lonely.",
      11: "In the eleventh house, Vesta devotes itself to friends, groups and collective ideals. You may dedicate yourself to a cause or a community, and you work well with like-minded people. You also need solitude within the group. The challenge is balancing service to the collective with close personal bonds. You may be the committed member who keeps a group going through lean times, long after others have drifted away. Choose communities whose values genuinely match your own, and you will give them your best without resentment.",
      12: "Vesta in the twelfth house focuses on the inner life, spirituality and service behind the scenes. You need a lot of solitude and may be drawn to retreat, meditation, healing or institutional work. Your devotion is often private. The work is bringing some of that inner flame out into the world, so your gifts can be shared. You may also have a talent for work that requires long concentration away from the public eye, such as research, writing or care in hospitals and retreats. Regular periods of withdrawal restore you."
    },
    aspects: {
      fusion: "A conjunction merges the planet's energy with your capacity for focus and devotion, so that area of life becomes something you give yourself to completely. It can also bring themes of solitude or sacred sexuality.",
      harmony: "Trines and sextiles help you focus the planet's energy with ease, making devotion in this area feel natural and sustaining.",
      tension: "Squares and oppositions create friction between your need for focused solitude and the planet's demands, often showing as a split between devotion and relationships or between work and life.",
      adjust: "A quincunx asks you to keep adjusting how you balance your focus with the planet's needs, often through changes in daily habits.",
      creative: "A quintile gives a distinctive talent for concentrating the planet's energy into a devoted, creative practice."
    },
    dominant: "When Vesta is prominent, conjunct the Sun, Moon or an angle, devotion and focus become central to your life. You may be deeply committed to a vocation, a spiritual path or a craft, and you may need more solitude than most people. Sexuality can carry special significance, whether as something sacred, private or channelled into your work. People sense your intensity and integrity. The work is keeping your flame alive without isolating yourself, so that your devotion warms the people around you as well as your chosen work."
  }
};
